{"id":"NCT02735707","title":"Randomized, Embedded, Multifactorial Adaptive Platform Trial for Community- Acquired Pneumonia","official":"Randomized, Embedded, Multifactorial Adaptive Platform Trial for Community- Acquired Pneumonia","summary":"REMAP-CAP is a randomised, embedded, multifactorial, adaptive platform trial for community-acquired pneumonia.\n\nThe purpose of this study is to evaluate the effect of a range of interventions to improve outcome of hospitalised patients admitted to intensive care with respiratory tract infections.\n\nIn addition, REMAP-CAP provides and adaptive research platform for evaluation of multiple treatment modalities in the event of a respiratory pandemic such as COVID-19.\n\nREMAP-COVID is a sub-platform of REMAP-CAP that evaluates treatments specific to COVID-19 in the United States of America.","conditions":["Respiratory Tract Diseases","Influenza (Pandemic)","Influenza","Community Acquired Pneumonia","Community Acquired Pneumonia (CAP)","Community Acquired Pneumonia, Severe","COVID-19","Respiratory Tract Infection Acute","Respiratory Tract Infections (RTI)","SARS CoV 2 Infection"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Ceftriaxone + Macrolide"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Moxifloxacin or Levofloxacin"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Piperacillin-tazobactam + Macrolide"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Ceftaroline + Macrolide"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Amoxicillin-clavulanate + Macrolide"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Standard course macrolide"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Extended course macrolide"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No systemic corticosteroid"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Fixed-duration Hydrocortisone"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Shock-dependent hydrocortisone"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Fixed-duration higher dose Hydrocortisone"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No antiviral agent for influenza"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Five-days oseltamivir"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Ten-days oseltamivir"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No antiviral agent for COVID-19"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Lopinavir / Ritonavir"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Hydroxychloroquine"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Hydroxychloroquine + lopinavir/ritonavir"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Ivermectin"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No immune modulation for COVID-19"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Interferon beta-1a"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Anakinra"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Tocilizumab"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Sarilumab"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Local standard venous thromboprophylaxis"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Therapeutic dose anticoagulation"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Conventional low dose thromboprophylaxis"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Intermediate dose thromboprophylaxis"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Continuation of therapeutic dose anticoagulation"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No immunoglobulin"},{"type":"BIOLOGICAL","name":"Convalescent plasma"},{"type":"BIOLOGICAL","name":"Delayed administration of convalescent plasma"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No vitamin C"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Vitamin C"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No antiplatelet"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Aspirin"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"P2Y12 inhibitor"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No simvastatin"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Simvastatin"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Eritoran"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Apremilast"},{"type":"PROCEDURE","name":"Clinician-preferred mechanical ventilation strategy"},{"type":"PROCEDURE","name":"Protocolised mechanical ventilation strategy"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No renin-angiotensin system inhibitor"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Angiotensin converting enzyme inhibitor"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Angiotensin Receptor Blockers"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"ARB + DMX-200"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No cysteamine"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Cysteamine"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Fixed-duration dexamethasone"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Baloxavir Marboxil"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Five-days oseltamivir + baloxavir marboxil"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Ten-days oseltamivir + baloxavir marboxil"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No endothelial modulator"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Imatinib"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No Immune Modulator for Influenza"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Tocilizumab"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Baricitinib"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No antiviral agent for COVID-19"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Nirmatrelvir/ritonavir"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Remdesivir"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Nirmatrelvir/ritonavir + remdesivir"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Amoxicillin-clavulanate + Ceftazidime + Macrolide"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Meropenem + Macrolide"}],"criteria":"The eligibility criteria for the Platform are applied at multiple levels. One level is that there are inclusion and exclusion criteria that determine eligibility for randomization within the Platform. Another level is that, once eligible for inclusion within the Platform, additional criteria (typically exclusion criteria) are applied that are specific to each domain. Finally, intervention-level eligibility criteria may be applied for interventions within a domain. A patient is eligible for inclusion within a domain when:\n\n* All Platform inclusion criteria are met\n* None of the Platform exclusion criteria are met\n* Domain-specific eligibility criteria are met\n* The patient is eligible for at least two interventions within a domain\n\nAs such, the key \"inclusion criteria\" for being eligible for a domain are that the patient is eligible for the Platform.\n\n\\--\n\nPLATFORM INCLUSION CRITERIA:\n\n1. Hospitalised patient\n2. Acute respiratory tract infection\n3. Aged 28 days or older\n\nPLATFORM EXCLUSION CRITERIA:\n\n1. Death is deemed to be imminent and inevitable during the next 24 hours AND one or more of the patient, substitute decision maker or attending physician are not committed to full active treatment\n2. Patient is expected to be discharged from hospital within the next 24 hours\n3. Previous participation in this REMAP within the last 90 days\n\nDOMAIN-SPECIFIC ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA:\n\nEach domain may have additional eligibility criteria. Refer to the study website for more information (www.remapcap.org).","minAge":"28 Days","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":20000,"start":"2016-04-11","pcd":"2028-06","upd":"2026-11-04","sponsor":"UMC Utrecht","areas":["oncology"],"central":["Cameron Green, MSc · info@remapcap.org","Svenja Peters, MSc · EU.remapcap@umcutrecht.nl"],"sites":[{"f":"Foothills Medical Centre","city":"Calgary","pr":"Alberta","zip":"T2W 1S7","s":"ANR","lat":51.0501,"lon":-114.0853,"c":""},{"f":"Peter Lougheed Centre","city":"Calgary","pr":"Alberta","zip":"T2W 1S7","s":"ANR","lat":51.0501,"lon":-114.0853,"c":""},{"f":"Rockyview General Hospital","city":"Calgary","pr":"Alberta","zip":"T2W 1S7","s":"ANR","lat":51.0501,"lon":-114.0853,"c":""},{"f":"South Health Campus","city":"Calgary","pr":"Alberta","zip":"T2W 1S7","s":"ANR","lat":51.0501,"lon":-114.0853,"c":""},{"f":"Royal Alexandra Hospital, Alberta","city":"Edmonton","pr":"Alberta","zip":"T5H 3V9","s":"R","lat":53.5501,"lon":-113.4687,"c":"Demetrios Kutsogiannis, MD"},{"f":"University of Alberta Hospital","city":"Edmonton","pr":"Alberta","zip":"T6G 2C8","s":"R","lat":53.5501,"lon":-113.4687,"c":"Wendy Sligl, MD"},{"f":"Surrey Memorial Hospital","city":"Surrey","pr":"British Columbia","zip":"V3V 1Z2","s":"NYR","lat":49.1063,"lon":-122.8251,"c":"Anish Mitra, MD"},{"f":"St Boniface General Hospital","city":"Winnipeg","pr":"Manitoba","zip":"R2H 2A6","s":"R","lat":49.8844,"lon":-97.147,"c":"Ryan Zarychanski, MD"},{"f":"Health Sciences Centre Winnipeg","city":"Winnipeg","pr":"Manitoba","zip":"R3A 1R9","s":"R","lat":49.8844,"lon":-97.147,"c":"Ryan Zarychanski, MD"},{"f":"Grace Hospital","city":"Winnipeg","pr":"Manitoba","zip":"R3J 3M7","s":"R","lat":49.8844,"lon":-97.147,"c":"Gloria Vazquez-Grande, MD"},{"f":"Dr. Everett Chalmers Regional Hospital","city":"Fredericton","pr":"New Brunswick","zip":"E3B 4R3","s":"NYR","lat":45.9454,"lon":-66.6656,"c":"Zeeshan Aslam, MD"},{"f":"The Moncton Hospital","city":"Fredericton","pr":"New Brunswick","zip":"E3